{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R8"],
      "pins": ["J3.B5", "R8.1", "R8.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(J3-CC2)", "GND"],
      "observed": "R8 is specified as 5.1M and connects USB-C receptacle CC2 (J3.B5) to GND. The SPICE deck also models R8 as 5.1Meg. Its listed MPN, 0603WAF5101T5E, instead indicates 5.1k, so the value and sourcing metadata conflict.",
      "expected": "A USB-C sink receptacle should have a 5.1kΩ Rd pull-down from each CC pin to GND; R8 should match R7's 5.1kΩ value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R8 | 5.1M | ... MPN=0603WAF5101T5E"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(J3-CC2) : J3.B5(CC2,bidirectional) R8.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND ... R8.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R7 | 5.1k"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R8 Net-_J3-CC2_ 0 5.1Meg"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the stated 5.1MΩ value is used, CC2 will not provide the required pull-down, so a USB-C source may fail to detect the board as a sink when the cable is connected in that orientation. The conflicting 5.1kΩ MPN makes the intended or assembled value ambiguous.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "R8 is modeled and specified as 5.1MΩ on USB-C CC2, rather than the required 5.1kΩ pull-down used on CC1. Its MPN conflicts with that value, creating both a likely orientation-dependent USB-C detection fault and a sourcing ambiguity."
}

